  "plainTakeaway": "Hand-written Playwright scripts remain the raw speed floor (~4.2s verified / 4.66s end-to-end across R1..R7 with 0 model calls), but require 72 SLOC (31 explicit Playwright selector/navigation ops) and fail on R6..R7 (5/7 completed) when Gate_v2 ships until a developer edits code (+11 SLOC). Upgrading stock automation with LLM-driven reusable helpers removes per-route manual scripting at the cost of 461 SLOC of custom helper/precondition/slice machinery, yet flat (startRoute, goal) helpers still cannot compose A->B + B->C or reconverge onto a shared suffix without asking the planner to pick and stitch call_helper slices—spending 30 vs 22 planner calls per repeat overall, and 17 vs 9 planner calls after R1..R2 teaching (-47.1% post-teaching calls in Fawn for the same 44/45 reused actions)."
